# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
# pytest scratch dir: it is currently unreadable (WinError 5) and, if committed,
# breaks test collection with a PermissionError before a single test runs.
aura/pytest-tmp/

# runtime state (regenerated on first run) — keep trained .npz models so
# judges can serve without training
aura/artifacts/aura.db
# Append-only audit log: every prediction adds a line, so tracking it made the
# tree dirty on any demo or test run. Created on demand by audit_log.py (append
# mode) and read behind an exists() guard, so a fresh clone is fine without it.
aura/artifacts/inference_log.jsonl

# editor/os noise
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# large datasets, zip archives, and manifests
archive.zip
mimic_cxr_data/
manifest.jsonl

# Per-study inference output — reports, Grad-CAM heatmaps, explanation HTML, one
# directory per study id. Regenerated on every run and specific to one upload on one
# machine. predictions/sample/ is the curated worked example and stays tracked;
# everything else under predictions/ is run output.
aura/artifacts/predictions/*
!aura/artifacts/predictions/sample/

# One-off debugging scripts from the import repair. search_struct.py greps a 48 MB
# local structure.txt that is itself gitignored, and show_safety_diff.py diffs a
# services/services/ path that no longer exists — neither runs on a fresh clone.
/search_struct.py
/show_safety_diff.py

# deep learning checkpoints / tensorboard logs
aura/artifacts/*.pt
aura/artifacts/tb/

# Training-resume state, never inference state. optimizer.pt is an optimiser's
# moment buffers and last_checkpoint.pt is the mid-run snapshot; only `train.py
# --resume` reads either. They were tracked at ~670 MB across five duplicated run
# directories, so every clone paid for them forever. The served weights are
# aura/artifacts/best_model.pt (and brain/checkpoints/best_brain_model.pt, fetched
# by deploy/fetch_models.py), which stay tracked and are what preflight checks.
**/optimizer.pt
**/last_checkpoint.pt

# Scratch output from `cli smoke` — two 161 MB copies of a throwaway run. Nothing in
# the codebase, the tests, the docs or the registries reads these paths.
aura/artifacts/_smoke/
aura/artifacts/_smoke2/

# Superseded brain run kept only as a curiosity: 400 MB of checkpoints whose quality
# head is known-broken (hence the directory name). Nothing references it. Retained on
# disk locally if anyone wants the post-mortem; it does not belong in every clone.
aura/artifacts/brain/v1_broken_quality_head/


# Brain Vision Engine (NeuroMind) — derived artefacts, all regenerable:
#   cache/        11 GB of standardised voxels; rebuild with `cli ingest`
#   checkpoints/  ~300 MB of weights; rebuild with `cli train`
#   embeddings/   one 3.5 MB store per epoch
# The reports, the model card, and the latest embedding store stay: they are the
# evidence, and `latest.npz` is the representation downstream modules are told not to
# recompute.
aura/artifacts/brain/cache/
aura/artifacts/brain/checkpoints/
aura/artifacts/brain/tensorboard/
aura/artifacts/brain/embeddings/epoch_*.npz

# IBM Quantum token — never commit (holds a real secret once filled)
ibm_quantum.env

# Local deployment overrides. .env.example is the committed template.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Datasets and large local data — never push (kept local, see E:\AURA root)
datasets/
demo_data/
/structure.txt

# A refactor tool once wrote a doubled-up copy of the source tree here
# (aura/change/common/common/, aura/change/gateway/gateway/, ...): 171 files and
# 28 kLOC that nothing imported, including a second copy of the evaluation pipeline
# that would silently miss any grep-and-fix. It has been moved to
# E:\AURA\_archived_change_tree_20260730\ and this rule stops it coming back —
# permanently untracked, it otherwise just buries the real entries in git status.
aura/change/
